Z||000008||Fformula88||06-05-2001||10:38 AM||||Ford missed a great opportunity with the new T-Bird.  They had a chance to create a truly great two seater roadster.  They only had to make it small, nimble and fast.  They did none of these.  This car is 190 inches long... only 3 inches short of my mom's Buick Century!  It also tips the scales at a minivan-like 3800+ pounds!!  I dunno about the rest of you, but it doesn't sounds like the makeup of a two seater roadster to me.<P>I've also seen this car in person at the auto show and it looks long.  Its lines all run front to back making it look gigantic in length.  I guess they forgot that the criticism of the Thunderbird was that it had gotten way too big.  <P>I am glad an American automaker had the guts to try building a nice niche vehicle.  However, for my 40K I'll take a Miata and save the extra $$ for lots of new tires to keep carving up the twisties!  (Or buy 10 Fiero's!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> )||||reg||1
Z||000009||saleenfiero||06-05-2001||01:10 PM||||Gotta ive kudos to these manufacturers for doing this, even if it is just for the money.  At least there will be some different looking cars on the road compared to the 40 billion SUVS and common sedans.  I don't really like the new beetle, cruiser and hate the new T-Bird, but the new Mini looks kick a$$!||||reg||1
