Z||000013||kslish||06-06-2001||04:48 PM||||The new T-bird is pretty overpriced in my opinion. Shouldn't be more than $30K.  I could think of a lot of other cars that I would much rather have if I could afford $35-$39K.  <P>What I want to see is some American company come out with a 2-seater sports car for around $20,000.  Just a basic fun car...not some luxo-barge.<P>Ken S.<BR>'87GT and '86SC <BR><A HREF="http://www.westpennfiero.org" TARGET=_blank>www.westpennfiero.org</A> <p>[This message has been edited by kslish (edited 06-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000014||84Bill||06-06-2001||06:44 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Butter:<BR><B>84Bill,<BR>If Ford would bring on the RS200 it Developed back in the 80's I bet Pontiac would get off its dead a$$.  I just feel like the engineers of the day for these big car companys have an unwriten code not to build anything that's as easily modified as say the late 60's muscle cars.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yeah one would think this in light of all the new 2 seat cars that have taken off like a shot since the demise of the Fiero. I mean<BR>what is Pontiacs problem anyway? So they got a bloody nose, big deal. Eddison was thaught to be insane for trieing to invent a lightbulb. The mentality at the time was why do we need a lightbulb candels work great! I know a car is not as important as a lightbulb but judging by the innovations brought forth by the design of the Fiero one has to wonder. I mean almost every car made today is in some way using the technologies from the manufacture and design of the Fiero.<P>Granted the Fiero would have undergone many changes brought about by our thieving caniving scheaming gonna get all your money and keep it to our self nofault bullsh!t (how the hell did they ever get away with nofault is beyond me) insurance industry such as the 45% offset impact, witch our beloved Fiero probably would not fare well at. But still can be overcome by a can do attitude that Ponti lost sight of.<P>Hindsight is 20/20 but they had an awesome concept with the Fiero judging by the numbers sold and if they just stuck it out IMAGINE what the Fiero would be today. It would be in its 2nd or 3rd generation by now and I'm sure a world class sports car and not just the commuter car of it's early days.<BR>Instead they try and try to burry the Fiero like an ugly stepchild instead of just fixing the problems (reported by the slanderous press) and moving farward. Yeah ok the suits cost them money but they sold 136000 units the FIRST YEAR OUT!!!!!!!! AND had the distinction of Paceing the indy 500 THE FIRST YEAR OUT!! with a 4 cylinder car no less! sheeesh what a feat that was. So now after all the BS Pontiac has laid out about not enough demand for 2 seat cars this and spent to much for recalls that. Here comes Ford with trucks that explode on side impacts and LTD's with bad steering gear and unintentional airbag deployments and a host of bad recall press, pops out with a big dopey 2 seat car and sells 20,000 before the first one rolls off the LINE! <P>COMON SNAP THE FORK OUT OF IT PONTIAC!! I (we) want a 2002 Fiero and I'll pay 30,000 for it as long as it has a mid engine the Fiero badge and the same spaceframe / outer panel construction. <P>Ok I think I popped a cork. <P>Thanks Butter for seeing the meaning of my post. I appriciate it   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR><p>[This message has been edited by 84Bill (edited 06-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000015||saleenfiero||06-06-2001||06:51 PM||||I'd said it before, I am intrigued by the notion of a new fiero, but I KNOW that it won't happen and I am kind of happy, our cars are unique for a reason.  All of us who can't afford a new fiero might lose its "coolness" after its stood up by the 21st century verison of the fiero, with its awesome engine, modern looks.  Did any of that make any sense?||||reg||1
Z||000016||84Bill||06-06-2001||06:58 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by saleenfiero:<BR><B>I'd said it before, I am intrigued by the notion of a new fiero, but I KNOW that it won't happen and I am kind of happy, our cars are unique for a reason.  All of us who can't afford a new fiero might lose its "coolness" after its stood up by the 21st century verison of the fiero, with its awesome engine, modern looks.  Did any of that make any sense?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Sure it makes sense but does this make sense to you? Your thinking short term, so you cant get a new 2002 Fiero ok wait till 2005 and get a 2002 Fiero. As far as coolness ask a split window vett owner if he feels uncool parked next to or blown away by a 2000 vett. I see your point. Yes very clearly.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000017||saleenfiero||06-06-2001||07:11 PM||||We're not comparing classics to modern marvels here, I'd take a split window vette over a 2001 Z06 in a mintue in a minute.  We're talking cool little sports cars with tons of unique attributes to the best Pontiac would have to offer in this day and age.  Fieros are great cars for expressing yourself, I'd sooner buy an old 87 or 88 and do it up over a 200X fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000018||84Bill||06-06-2001||07:33 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by saleenfiero:<BR><B>We're not comparing classics to modern marvels here, I'd take a split window vette over a 2001 Z06 in a mintue in a minute.  We're talking cool little sports cars with tons of unique attributes to the best Pontiac would have to offer in this day and age.  Fieros are great cars for expressing yourself, I'd sooner buy an old 87 or 88 and do it up over a 200X fiero.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The Fiero IS a and can be classified as a Classic car according to PA DMV. However should Ponti have kept building the Fiero I'm sure early Fieros would be even MORE scarce than they are right now and the value would be much much greater for the early models. Lets face it why would I own an older Fiero when I could get a newer one. <BR>Sure wish I had a sweet 74 Mustang II 4 banger like a friend of mine does or even his mint 74 4 door Chevy Impalla smogged out 100 hp 305  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> It's just a matter of time thats all.||||reg||1
